B.VU=new A.aW(B.WV,["Splendid. Now all we want is the weapon.",u.h,u.p,u.X,u.Q,u.Q,u.o,"The operator vouches for her, and I believe it. But she was stood on that landing for forty minutes with her ears open. What did she hear from downstairs?",u.N,"Fourteen pounds of iron, gone from Penny's kitchen. She counts her wooden spoons, Churlock. She will know who had it last.","One glass used and one not. So one of the two at that board drank, and one only poured. Ask Penny what is purple, full of seeds, and smells of the nursery.","Thirty years of books, and the keys to be given up at breakfast. I wonder what an auditor would have found.","Wrapped up and put away tidily, by somebody who knows where the linen lives. Dust it.","Put out of sight in a hurry, by somebody who passed through the hall. Dust it.","Two sets of books. That is not a grievance, old chap, that is a prison sentence, and it was due at nine this morning.","Every Friday for thirty years. That is not a grievance, old chap, that is a prison sentence, and it was due at nine this morning.","Sleep follows. Three fingers gone. Ask Penny who asked her for that bottle, and what reason they gave.","A man does not drool on a chair wing while he is winning at chess. Ask him how the game went. Then ask somebody who could hear it.","Crumbs like those turn up in the pantry every day, and innocently. But these are in the cellar, and on top of the custard.","Still hot when it was put down. So it came straight from wherever irons are kept hot. Who had the irons last night?","Play it through in your head, Churlock, move by move. Every move ought to be possible.","Hers are old and where a laundress's belong. His is fresh, and on the part nobody touches unless they are wiping it."],t.l)
B.Ru=s(["Two of them say they sat at a chessboard together all night, Churlock. That is two alibis resting on one another. Was anybody else in a position to hear that game?","Look at the two glasses on the chess table, and then look in Penny's cupboard. One of those two players was not awake for all of it.","If one of them slept, the other was alone, and wrote the record of the game by himself. Ask for that record and read every move.","The Colonel snored, and Tira heard him. Nobody heard the butler. And a queen that is taken at move fifteen does not give check at move twenty-four."],t.s)
B.ae5=new A.m("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. Pressed, Detective. Flat as a napkin, and as smooth. Whatever did it was heavy, and it was hot. We traced where she lay in powdered sugar.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.abh=new A.m("weapon","What was the weapon?","Something flat and heavy with a handle on top. If this were a laundry I'd know exactly what to look for. It isn't down here.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.OX=s([B.ae5,B.abh,B.dG,B.cF],t.q)
B.abZ=new A.m("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, but fair. She paid on time and never once called me \u201cjelly\u201d. She'd taken to going through the books of an evening, this last month. Every bill since the year dot.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.Sg=s(["ironrack"],t.s)
B.aec=new A.m("iron","Your biggest flat iron is missing.","The goose! Fourteen pounds, that iron. Graham carried all three through to the dining room at ten, to press the napkins and tomorrow's Gazette. He brought two back hot at half eleven and said the goose was cooling. I never thought.",B.Sg,B.c,null)
B.RZ=s(["glasses","syrup"],t.s)
B.aev=new A.m("syrup","What is purple, full of seeds, and smells of the nursery?","My poppy-seed syrup. One spoonful and you sleep the clock round. Graham asked me for the bottle at ten. He said Madam had a cough. Madam never coughed in her life, now I come to think.",B.RZ,B.c,null)
B.Oz=s([B.cS,B.abZ,B.jn,B.aec,B.aev,B.dF,B.cL,B.dM,B.cR,B.cQ,B.cU,B.cT],t.q)
B.aer=new A.m("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, sir, at chess with the Colonel, from half past ten until two minutes to midnight. Neither of us left the board. The Colonel was in unusually fine form.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.Kt=new A.O("scoresheet","Chess Scoresheet","",0,"Graham's record of the game, a move every two or three minutes from 10:32 to 11:58, each one initialled twice. Among them: \u201cMove 15, 10:47. Bishop takes the Colonel's queen.\u201d And further down: \u201cMove 24, 11:12. The Colonel's queen to king seven. Check.\u201d The Colonel wins at move 41.",B.ll,B.J,null,B.k,B.c,!1,"graham")
B.abF=new A.m("record","Is there a record of the game?","Every move, sir, timed and initialled by both players. I should be obliged if you would return it. It was one of the Colonel's better evenings and he will wish to frame it.",B.c,B.c,B.Kt)
B.qw=s(["glasses"],t.s)
B.aex=new A.m("glasses","Only one of the brandy glasses was used.","The Colonel takes a nightcap, sir. I do not drink while I am in livery. I poured it for him myself at half past ten.",B.qw,B.c,null)
B.Qh=s(["penny/syrup"],t.s)
B.aew=new A.m("syrup","Penny says you borrowed her sleeping syrup.","For Madam's cough, sir. I left the bottle on her tray. If some of it found its way into the brandy, I can only suppose the Colonel mistook it for a liqueur.",B.c,B.Qh,null)
B.qR=s(["tira/heard"],t.s)
B.acE=new A.m("snore","Tira heard snoring from the parlor, and no chess.","The Colonel breathes heavily when he concentrates, sir. It is frequently mistaken for sleep. He was thinking.",B.c,B.qR,null)
B.abW=new A.m("queen","The Colonel's queen is taken at move 15 and moves at 24.","A slip of the pen, sir. One writes \u201cqueen\u201d for \u201crook\u201d late in the evening. The Colonel initialled it, you will observe.",B.cz,B.c,null)
B.Nm=s(["penny/iron"],t.s)
B.adr=new A.m("iron","You had all three irons in the dining room.","I iron Madam's newspaper each morning, sir, and the napkins at night. I returned the irons to Mrs. Cotta when I had done. If she counted two, I can only say that the hour was late.",B.c,B.Nm,null)
B.Re=s(["cornerprint","scorch"],t.s)
B.adz=new A.m("crumb","Your crumbs are in the cellar, on top of the custard.","I am in the cellar daily, sir, to keep the book. I shed. It is a condition of being what I am.",B.Re,B.c,null)
B.T4=s(["realbooks","passbook"],t.s)
B.abO=new A.m("books","You have put away 31,000 sugar cubes.","Thirty years of prudent saving, sir, and a small legacy from an aunt in Shortbread. I should be glad to explain it to any auditor.",B.T4,B.c,null)
B.aby=new A.m("auditor","The auditor was to take your keys this morning.","Madam mentioned it, sir. I welcomed it. A butler's books should bear inspection.",B.lH,B.c,null)
B.adQ=new A.m("prints","Your thumb is on the sole of the iron.","I test the heat with my thumb, sir. Every butler does. It is how one avoids scorching The Gazette.",B.aY,B.c,null)
B.QR=s([B.aer,B.dH,B.h7,B.abF,B.CB,B.aex,B.aew,B.acE,B.abW,B.adr,B.adz,B.abO,B.aby,B.adQ,B.cJ,B.cM,B.cK,B.cW,B.cX,B.cV],t.q)
B.acD=new A.m("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, at chess with Graham, half ten to midnight. Played like a tiger, sir! The fellow tells me I won. First time in eleven years.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.ac1=new A.m("nightcap","Tell me about your nightcap.","Graham poured it, sir, at half past ten. Dashed sweet, I thought. Purple, too. I took it for a new bottle and said nothing. One doesn't criticise another man's cellar.",B.qw,B.c,null)
B.ad2=new A.m("doze","Tira heard you snoring for forty minutes.","Snoring? I may have rested my eyes, sir. A soldier sleeps when he can. One moment Graham was pouring, and the next he was saying \u201cYour move, sir,\u201d and the clock stood at half past eleven. ...Good Lord.",B.c,B.qR,null)
B.aed=new A.m("queen","Do you remember giving check with your queen?","My queen, sir? I lost her early. I remember that distinctly, because I said a word one doesn't say in front of a butler. I never got her back. Did I check him with her? I have no memory of it at all.",B.cz,B.c,null)
B.Tq=s([B.acD,B.h9,B.n_,B.ac1,B.ad2,B.aed,B.eG,B.eF,B.jm,B.cH,B.dJ],t.q)
B.acX=new A.m("suspect","Who do you suspect?","The Colonel, darling. He owes Auntie a fortune and he has the manners of a man who knows it.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.adY=new A.m("heard","What could you hear from the parlor during your call?","The Colonel, darling, snoring like a kettle with a grudge. From about a quarter to eleven until nearly half past. Not one \u201ccheck\u201d, not one \u201cwhat\u201d. I assumed Graham had bored him unconscious.",B.ej,B.c,null)
B.Sf=s(["ironchest"],t.s)
B.abq=new A.m("footsteps","Did anyone pass you on the landing?","Not then, darling. But somebody came up to the linen chest after I'd rung off and gone to my room. A very neat, square sort of tread.",B.Sf,B.c,null)
B.U0=s([B.eE,B.dL,B.acX,B.adY,B.abq,B.dI,B.dN,B.cG,B.cY],t.q)
B.aeu=new A.m("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Butler's had the keys to this place thirty year, guv, and the old girl had just started askin' where the coal money went. I only know 'cause she asked me.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.OT=s([B.eD,B.cI,B.aeu,B.cZ,B.cN,B.cP,B.cO,B.dK],t.q)
B.VM=new A.aW(B.dw,[B.OX,B.is,B.Oz,B.QR,B.Tq,B.U0,B.OT],t.wU)
